WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.190
Did the Star Wars sequel trilogy give us one
Big Bad for the price of two?

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:09.820
With the release of Star Wars: The Rise of
Skywalker imminent, the rumor mill is working

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:14.660
overtime - and the latest nugget has to do
with the late Supreme Leader Snoke, Emperor

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.880
Palpatine, and the relationship between the
two characters.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:22.640
The rumor comes from fan site Making Star
Wars, which has been a fairly reliable source

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:27.960
of inside information - so be warned that
potential spoilers for Rise of Skywalker are

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:28.460
ahead.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:33.620
Ever since his first appearance in Star Wars:
The Force Awakens, the identity of Snoke has

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.320
been shrouded in mystery.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:39.640
Where did he come from, how did he come to
assume control of the First Order after the

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.160
fall of the Empire, and what is his interest
in Kylo Ren?

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:49.300
Rise of Skywalker will presumably answer all
of those questions, but Making Star Wars might

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.999
have answered one of them for us just a little
bit early.

00:00:51.999 --> 00:00:56.020
The website's alleged spoiler has to do with
a scene that supposedly takes place on the

00:00:56.020 --> 00:01:00.280
dead planet of Exogol, where Emperor Palpatine
has been in hiding.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.800
"Wait," you say, stroking your chin.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:04.700
"I thought he died!"

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:05.720
"No!

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:07.680
NO!

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:08.500
NO!

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:09.860
YOU will die!"

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.140
Geez, grandpa - take a chill pill.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:20.140
But yeah, no, we still have no explanation
as to just how ol' Palps has returned.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.220
For the purposes of this rumor, however, it's
neither here nor there.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:29.540
The Emperor is confronted by Kylo Ren, whom
we assume has located the old dude with the

00:01:29.549 --> 00:01:34.119
help of one of those heavily rumored "Wayfinder"
devices that are said to be central to the

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:34.840
flick's plot.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:40.720
Ren is skeptical that Palpatine even is who
he says he is, but he's shaken to discover

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:45.580
that the Emperor is keeping several clones
of Snoke in vats in his lair.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:51.640
Their conversation becomes more and more confrontational,
with Ren's anger starting to bubble to the

00:01:51.649 --> 00:01:56.270
surface, and Palpatine becoming more and more
annoyed that this young upstart doesn't grasp

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:58.020
the enormity of what's going on here.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:05.680
When Ren finally invokes Snoke by name, Palpatine
makes a startling proclamation: "I am Snoke!"

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:11.360
Well, we didn't see that coming... okay, maybe
we sort of saw it coming, but we were never

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:12.340
exactly sure.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:16.480
The question that remains, though - assuming
that this rumor is accurate, and that this

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:21.200
scene actually exists - is whether or not
Palpatine is speaking literally.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:25.980
Could it be that Palpatine has actually found
a way to transfer his consciousness into the

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:27.180
body of another being?

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:33.200
This might explain why Snoke was so keen to
groom Ren; perhaps the young guy was actually

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.680
being prepped to become Palpatine's next vessel.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:40.920
Hey, if we were trapped inside that horrifying
bag of bones that was Snoke, we'd be keen

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:45.640
to hook ourselves up with a younger, far more
aesthetically pleasing - and broad-shouldered

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:46.560
- body, too.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:51.320
However, don't forget that Palpatine has employed
this phrasing before, during the events of

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:53.200
Star Wars: Revenge of the Sith.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:58.440
While still holding the title of Supreme Chancellor,
and before his transformation into a walking,

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:03.939
breathing jump scare, Palpatine was confronted
by Jedi Master Mace Windu over having concealed

00:03:03.939 --> 00:03:06.690
his identity as the Sith Lord Darth Sidious.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:11.459
Attempting to place Palpatine under arrest,
Windu informs him that "the Senate will decide

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:16.380
[his] fate," whereupon Palpatine coolly replies,
"I am the Senate."

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:21.079
Obviously, Palpatine is prone to speaking
in such metaphorical terms, and it's pretty

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:25.220
likely that in revealing his relationship
to Snoke, he's doing so again.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:30.520
Rather than admitting to having physical control
over the Supreme Leader, he's instead simply

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:36.070
stating that Snoke was his puppet - a puppet
which he happens to have several copies of,

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:39.300
laying around in vats, which Ren can plainly
see.

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:43.920
Of course, it must be reiterated that this
report should be taken not with a grain of

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:46.440
salt, but with several heaping tablespoons.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:51.840
Making Star Wars' sources are as anonymous
as sources get, and while their description

00:03:51.849 --> 00:03:56.239
of this scene is pretty darn detailed, that
still doesn't preclude the possibility that

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:59.140
someone pulled it wholesale straight out of
their keisters.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:04.620
If it is accurate, though, it may help to
explain a few things - such as the degenerated,

00:04:04.629 --> 00:04:09.550
unsettlingly melt-y look of Snoke, and why
the heck the Supreme Leader was so easily

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:12.960
and unceremoniously killed halfway through
The Last Jedi.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:18.360
We find it pretty easy to believe that that
old puppetmaster Palpatine has been laying

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:22.300
low, pulling strings throughout the sequel
films - so we're going to go ahead and rate

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.770
this rumor "Seems Pretty Legit."

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:29.760
Fortunately, we don't have too long to wait
to find out whether we're right: Star Wars:

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:34.940
The Rise of Skywalker, the conclusion to the
nine-film Skywalker Saga, finally hits the

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:36.380
big screen on December 20.

